The train finally reached Lonavala station.
I put my own bag on my back.
I got off the train.
There was a big crowd of people on the platform.
But the outside air was completely different.
The temperature here was much lower than Mumbai.
I felt a cool breeze.
I took a deep breath.
I felt very refreshed.
Then, I saw a stall on the platform.
That vendor was selling Lonavala's famous chikki.
I walked up to him.
I said, "Dada, give me one packet of peanut chikki."
He took out a packet from his shop.
He gave that packet to me.
I asked him, "How much is this?"
He said, "Eighty rupees, madam."
I gave him the money.
I kept that chikki in my own bag.
Now I was ready to go towards the hill.
